{
  "$comment": "Chrome on macOS edits text with the system's key bindings (NSResponder selectors), which a key sent over CDP does not trigger: the engine names them on the key event (Input.dispatchKeyEvent `commands`) when its Chrome runs on one of `platforms`. Keys: modifiers in the order Shift, Control, Alt, Meta, then the key (a letter in lower case, or the DOM key name). Values: Blink editing command names (a selector without its colon). insert* selectors are left out: the key's own text does that.",
